From: hanson@hss.caltech.edu (Robin Hanson)
Date: Thu, 15 Sep 1994 10:56:29 -0700
Subject: [#94-9-140] Memetics

I (Robin Hanson) wrote:
>For example, urges to procreate are likely under the firm control of
>genes, and should remain regardless of how memetic evolution goes, as
>long as genes continue evolving as they have.  But opinions on how
>long to wear your hair are likely to be under pretty weak genetic control.
>
>Of course once we have uploads and/or substantial conscious/techno
>control of our genes the whole gene/meme relation will change
>dramatically.  This is an issue that deserves some careful thought.

Marvin Minsky writes:
>We now can design systems based on new kinds of "unnatural
>selection" that can exploit explicit plans and goals, and can also exploit
>the inheritance of acquired characteristics.  ...
>
>It simply means that once the meme-systems get advanced enough, like ours,
>then some of us can decide that we'd rather have immortality than lots of
>children.  Now, snip out those silly genes that inflict upon us those
>urges to procreate.  Maybe alter them for better hair-growing.  Time to
>start thinking, now: Down With Genes!

How about a little more respect for your elders before you enslave or
kill them?  :-)  Actually, technically, "genes" would still be in
charge, we would just become them!  Better to say "Down with DNA!". 

Until now, DNA "genotypes" (meaning what natural selection works
directly on) coded for brain structure and other body "phenotypes"
(meaning what genotypes induce in individual bodies), which strongly
encouraged certain human values to appear in dynamic human mental
structures. 

Now what if soon human minds can directly choose the DNA in their own
bodies and of their designer-DNA children, or are uploaded into new
designed hardware and are copied as whole mental units, with these
choices now made on the basis of human values and beliefs encoded in
dynamic mental structures?  Then suddenly dynamic human mental
structures become the new "genotypes", with DNA or new hardware
expressions becoming the new "phenotypes"!  Our minds, and not our
DNA, would be the new "genes", the new units of natural selection.

Now for any given human DNA there has been substantial variation in
human values from one human to another, a variation in part forced on
DNA genes but perhaps also encouraged to some degree by DNA genes.
This variation becomes the root of a feeling of "liberation" in minds,
since their particular values, and not the mean values encouraged by
their DNA, will now determine their particular future lineage.  

But of course natural selection will continue.  While Marvin feels
liberated to focus on immortality at the expense of procreation,
others will feel liberated to focus on procreation at the expense of
other stuff.  Natural selection will decide which values will come to
dominate the future.  And have a little respect for the DNA you are
replacing -- the apple doesn't fall too far from the tree, and your
current values really are not too far from what your DNA had in mind.

